        "original_id": "ddb47080-67f4-5a4d-a6da-8cc301d45207",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jimi Mistry, Nonso Anozie, Guy Ritchie, Om Puri, Linda Bassett, Gerard Butler, Tom Wilkinson, Thandie Newton, Mark Strong, Idris Elba, Tom Hardy, Toby Kebbell\n- Films and TV series: EastEnders, Coronation Street, East Is East, Blood Diamond, The Guru, Exam, West Is West, Ella Enchanted, The Truth About Love, RocknRolla, Ender's Game, Zoo, Game of Thrones\n- Places: Salford, Lancashire\n- Roles: George, Ella, Tank, Sergeant Dap, Abraham Kenyatta, Xaro Xhoan Daxos\n\nFacts:\n- Jimi Mistry was born on 1 January 1973 and is an English actor.\n- East Is East is set in Salford, Lancashire, in 1971 in a mixed-ethnicity British household headed by Pakistani father George, played by Om Puri, and English mother Ella, played by Linda Bassett.\n- East Is East is a film in which Jimi Mistry appeared.\n- RocknRolla is a 2008 British-American crime comedy film written and directed by Guy Ritchie.\n- RocknRolla stars Gerard Butler, Tom Wilkinson, Thandie Newton, Mark Strong, Idris Elba, Tom Hardy, Jimi Mistry, and Toby Kebbell.\n- Jimi Mistry is best known for roles in EastEnders and Coronation Street and for appearing in films including Blood Diamond, The Guru, Exam, West Is West, Ella Enchanted, and The Truth About Love.\n- Nonso Anozie is best known for playing Tank in RocknRolla, Sergeant Dap in Ender's Game, Abraham Kenyatta in Zoo, and Xaro Xhoan Daxos in the HBO television series Game of Thrones.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
